# Apple iOS Design

Follow Apple Human Interface Guidelines:
https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/

Before implementing a screen:

1. Identify the primary user goal
2. Identify the primary action
3. Identify secondary actions
4. Determine the iOS navigation pattern
5. Choose inline, grouped, sheet, full-screen, or alert
6. Use system typography
7. Use semantic colors
8. Plan VoiceOver, Dynamic Type, contrast, 44pt targets, Reduce Motion
9. Plan haptics (selective)
10. Plan fast, subtle animation

Prefer Cupertino widgets. Do not blindly use Material.

Tokens live in `AppColors`, `AppTypography`, `AppSpacing`, `AppRadius`, `AppElevation`, `AppMotion`. Do not scatter visual constants.

Tab bar: Home, Workout, Nutrition, Coach, Progress. Profile is secondary.

Home answers "What should I do today?"

Active workout is the highest UX priority: large targets, minimal typing, one-handed use.

Coach is not a ChatGPT clone. Show insight cards, then conversation, then structured Apply/Dismiss actions.

Materials only on tab/nav bars. Content cards stay opaque. Honor Reduce Motion. Never indicate status with color alone.

After each screen, review as an Apple designer and simplify if needed.
